{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 34,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Furthermore Elihu answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear my words, O ye wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; and give ear to me, ye that have knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the ear trieth words, as the mouth tasteth food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us choose to us judgment: let us know among ourselves what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Job hath said, I am righteous: and God hath taken away my judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should I lie against my right? my wound ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " incurable without transgression.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like Job, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " drinketh up scorning like water?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who goeth in company with the workers of iniquity, and walketh with wicked men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he hath said, It profiteth a man nothing that he should delight himself with God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore hearken to me, ye men of understanding: far be it from God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that he should do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wickedness; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Almighty, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that he should commit",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the work of a man he shall render to him, and cause every man to find according to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, surely God will not do wickedly, neither will the Almighty pervert judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath given him a charge over the earth? or who hath disposed the whole world?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he should set his heart upon man, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he should gather to himself his spirit and his breath;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All flesh would perish together, and man would turn again to dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou hast",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " understanding, hear this: hearken to the voice of my words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall even he that hateth right govern? and wilt thou condemn him that is most just?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is it fit",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to say to a king, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thou art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wicked? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to princes, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ye are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ungodly?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much less to him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that accepteth not the persons of princes, nor regardeth the rich more than the poor? for they all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the work of his hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In a moment they shall die, and the people shall be troubled at midnight, and pass away: and the mighty shall be taken away without hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For his eyes ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon the ways of man, and he seeth all his goings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no darkness, nor shadow of death, where the workers of iniquity may hide themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he will not lay upon man more ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "than right",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; that he should enter into judgment with God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall break in pieces mighty men without number, and set others in their stead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore he knoweth their works, and he overturneth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the night, so that they are destroyed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He striketh them as wicked men in the open sight of others;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because they turned back from him, and would not consider any of his ways:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that they cause the cry of the poor to come to him, and he heareth the cry of the afflicted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he giveth quietness, who then can make trouble? and when he hideth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " face, who then can behold him? whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it be done",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against a nation, or against a man only:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the hypocrite may not reign, lest the people should be ensnared.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely it is meet to be said to God, I have borne ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "chastisement",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I will not offend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I see not teach thou me: if I have done iniquity, I will do no more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should it be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " according to thy mind? he will recompense it, whether thou shalt refuse, or whether thou shalt choose; and not I: therefore speak what thou knowest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let men of understanding tell me, and let a wise man hearken to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Job hath spoken without knowledge, and his words ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My desire ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Job may be tried to the end, because of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " answers for wicked men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.34.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he addeth rebellion to his sin, he clappeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his hands",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among us, and multiplieth his words against God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
